created: undefined, last updated: 2026-07-20, [Read more](https://files-sdk.dev/docs/ui/server/tanstack-start)

Mount the Files gateway in a TanStack Start server route.
createRouteHandler returns { GET, POST, PUT } over the Web Request - Web-native, runs on every deploy target.
`files-sdk/tanstack-start` mounts a `createFilesRouter` in a TanStack Start server route.
TanStack Start hands each method handler a Web `Request` on `{ request }`, so — like `files-sdk/next` — `createRouteHandler` returns a `{ GET, POST, PUT }` handlers object: `GET` serves downloads, `POST` the JSON verbs, and `PUT` the upload byte path.
The handlers are Web-native, so the route runs on **every TanStack Start deployment target**.
